  "id": "adequate",
  "neon": "#ff8a2e",
  "note": "Marrow Street’s anchor and the only thing on that strip with four floors. A department store sets BACK rather than twists — three diminishing storeys over a deep shopfront podium, a centred chamfered attic and the corner rotunda on top, which is what a store of this kind actually puts there. ⚠ ITS NEON STAYS SODIUM ON PURPOSE. Everything west of here burns magenta or cyan now; this is the middle of the gradient, and the warm sign is how the street says so without a coordinate being named anywhere in the renderer. ⚠ A CANTILEVER AND A ROTATION NEVER SHARE A SEGMENT — see the warning in aurelia.json. An offset box and a yawed box are each safe; a box that is both puts the derived kit where its own solid is not, and glself catches it. So asymmetry here is offset-only and every chamfer is CENTRED. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the deptstore arm back.",
